\title{The algebraic numbers}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Taking #{K = \mathbb{Q}} and #{L = \mathbb{C}} we see that #{\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \lbrace \text{algebraic numbers}\rbrace } is a field. Since #{\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \supset \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt[d]{2})} and #{[\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt[d]{2}):\mathbb{Q}] = d} for all #{d}, we see that #{[\overline{\mathbb{Q}}:\mathbb{Q}] = \infty}.}
